# Security-owned paths (PR5-SEC-04, PR2-SEC-08; ADR-0023 am. J item 2 (b), D-ARCH-003 rev 4, data-model §8.3 rule 12,
# threat-model T-107/R-21). In this single-maintainer repository, "CODEOWNERS review" for these paths means the lane A
# check tools/ci/check-security-owned-paths.mjs: a PR that changes any path below needs a committed security review
# record docs/05-quality/security/PR-<nnnn>-*.md that names a commit of the PR after which no security-owned path
# changed, with a verdict other than FAIL. The check runs from the base ref and reads this file from both the base
# and the head, so removing a line here does not exempt the PR that removes it.

# CI, workflows, supply chain
/.github/                               @sukhchdit
/.npmrc                                 @sukhchdit
/package.json                           @sukhchdit
/package-lock.json                      @sukhchdit
/tools/ci/                              @sukhchdit
/tools/deps/                            @sukhchdit
/tools/hooks/                           @sukhchdit
/tools/isolated/                        @sukhchdit

# Static-analysis controls (lint, Semgrep, Gitleaks)
/eslint.config.mjs                      @sukhchdit
/stylelint.config.mjs                   @sukhchdit
/.gitignore                             @sukhchdit
/.semgrepignore                         @sukhchdit
/.stylelintignore                       @sukhchdit
/.gitleaks.toml                         @sukhchdit
/.semgrep/                              @sukhchdit
/tools/eslint-rules/                    @sukhchdit
/tools/stylelint-rules/                 @sukhchdit
/tools/lint/                            @sukhchdit
/tests/fixtures/lint/                   @sukhchdit
/tests/fixtures/semgrep/                @sukhchdit

